    "result_text": "All 54 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI replaced the direct level-computation rule with a points-based system across three files:\n\n**`Owner.java`** \u2014 replaced the old `getMembershipLevel()` (which started at 1 and capped intermediate factors at 3) with two methods:\n- `getMembershipPoints()` \u2014 starts at 0; `+2` email present, `+1` namesakeCount is 0, `+2` household of 3+, `+3` tenure over 365 days.\n- `getMembershipLevel()` \u2014 now derived from points: `1` (0\u20131), `2` (2\u20133), `3` (4\u20135), `4` (6+).\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the `membershipPoints` schema property and updated the `membershipLevel` description/constraints (now max 4). This regenerates `OwnerDto` with the new field.\n\n**Mapper** \u2014 no change needed; MapStruct maps `membershipPoints` by name from the new getter automatically, so both fields are returned in the response.\n\nThe previously-failing acceptance tests (Cp15, Cp23, Cp24, Cp40 asserting `membershipPoints`, plus the level-mapping tests) now pass, and no existing test regressed.",
